  "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm \\pi ,\\,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\,\\pm 3\\pi ,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\\pm 3\\pi ,\u2026}.\n$$",
